  "family": "jazz",
  "lineage": "1980s-and-onward American-Jewish jazz-fusion style integrating klezmer modal-and-melodic vocabulary with jazz-improvisational practice. Don Byron's Plays the Music of Mickey Katz (1993) and the Klezmatics 1980s-onward recordings constitute the canonical type-specimens; the parallel Frank London-led ensembles and David Krakauer's solo work extended the genre. Distinguished from broader klezmer revival by jazz-fusion's explicit jazz-improvisation-and-harmonic emphasis.",
  "recipe": "classic North American mid-1980s klezmer-jazz fusion, improv On Frame, klezmer improv branch, Jewish ritual devotional matrouz and piyyut abayudaya music. thick, breath veiled tone, straight onset, interlocked note trading. ebonite hard rubber klezmer tradition clarinet, alto phosphor bronze selmer mark vi canonical 1954 1974 jazz paris continuous-airflow legato saxophone, cold pressed light felt practice grade oversize maple tension resonator grand piano, growly gut upright bass, vintage ambassador asymmetric brushes-and-sticks drum kit, klezmer ensemble. nuyorican fania canon 1968-1977 mid tier fania la tierra studios ny. large-diaphragm condenser, Neve 1073 inductor pre, SSL inline console, dbx 160 VCA, SSL surgical EQ. Studer 30ips tape plate reverb digital delay.",
